earch and solutions to real-world problems are cornerstones of our educational programs which lead to new knowledge, therapies, and devices and well-prepared students ready to positively impact the world.\nRowan engineer to accept 2026 Edison Patent Award\n8/20/26 - Professor Beachley will be honored this fall with a 2026 Edison Patent Award in the \u201cAdvanced Manufacturing\u201d category.\nResearchers turn lab discovery into startup\n8/19/26 - HydroPep Therapeutics is developing an injectable material designed to stimulate new bone growth and improve healing after fractures.\n3D printing to study bone cancer cell behavior\n8/5/26 - Professor Vernengo uses 3D cell printing to study cell interactions to better understand a treatment resistant bone cancer.\nFollow Rowan BME\nHenry M. Rowan College of Engineering\nBack to Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering\nMain Menu\nBiomedical Engineering (BME)\nMessage From The Chair\nAbout Us\nContacts\nCampus Map & Directions\nAccreditation\nFaculty & Staff\nUndergraduate Programs\nB.S. in BME\nCurriculum\nAccelerated Programs\nDegree Program Enrichments\nCertificates of Undergraduate Study\nGraduate Program\nM.S. Program\nPh.D. Program\nMaster of Translational Orthopedic Device Engineering\nMD/Ph.D. Program\nDO/Ph.D. Program\nEngineering Clinics\nResearch\nProspective Students\nOutreach\nBEAM\nRISER\nNews\nBME News\nStudent Spotlight\nRowan on LinkedIn\nRowan on Facebook\nRowan on Instagram\nRowan on YouTube\nRowan on Tiktok\nRowan University \u2022 201 Mullica Hill Road \u2022 Glassboro, New Jersey 08028 \u2022 856-256-4000\n\u00a92026 Rowan University. Consumer Disclosures | Legal Notices | University Catalog\nRead the Notice of Availability of Rowan\u2019s Annual Security & Fire Safety Report", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://engineering.rowan.edu/programs/biomedical/#main"], ["News", "https://today.rowan.edu/index.html"], ["Alumni", "https://www.alumni.rowan.edu/s/1653/02-alumni/start.aspx?gid=2&pgid=61"], [